{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "18", "m": "08", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "08", "M": "20", "S": "59"}}, "news": [{"title": "Bhopal civic body issues 6,800 notices, to crack down on illegal commercial use", "para": "Bhopal Municipal Corporation is intensifying its crackdown on commercial activities in residential properties.  Around 6,800 notices have been issued, with a final 24-hour notice now being served.  Premises continuing unauthorized commercial activity after the deadline may face sealing by authorities.  The drive began on August 9 following a Supreme Court order.  Civic body teams are inspecting over 62,000 properties for violations.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/regulatory/bhopal-civic-body-issues-6800-notices-to-crack-down-on-illegal-commercial-use/133312006?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-108826/133312006.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "regulatory"}, {"title": "Greater Noida flat owner gets parking space denied to him after eight-year battle in consumer court", "para": "After an arduous eight-year legal struggle, a Noida flat owner finally secured his long-awaited parking space. The consumer court's ruling mandated the developer to fulfill their commitment, particularly after the developer contested an earlier decision. Recognizing the developer's shortcomings in service, the court awarded the rightful parking space to the flat owner, bringing resolution to this drawn-out case.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/greater-noida-flat-owner-gets-parking-space-denied-to-him-after-eight-year-battle-in-consumer-court/133311882?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-1855785/133311882.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}, {"title": "DTCP rejects AIPL plea against Oberoi Realty\u2019s Gurugram project", "para": "The Haryana DTCP has held that Licence No. 69 of 2025 and the June 17, 2025 approval for change of developer in favour of Oberoi Realty are legally intact. Oberoi Realty said the restriction imposed by the Punjab & Haryana High Court on fresh allotments and creation of third-party rights has ceased to be operative.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/regulatory/dtcp-rejects-aipl-plea-against-oberoi-realtys-gurugram-project/133311763?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-43466/133311763.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "regulatory"}]}